  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(1)=2\\,\u27f9\\,y=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(3)-(1)=3\\,\u27f9\\,x=3+4=7.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=7$,  $y=3$,  and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e87,3,1\u27e9.$",
